WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.373 --> 00:00:09.354
Shifts shows who’s on duty, plans the week, and records how it went. In this video, you’ll see your own shifts, the team schedule, and how people clock in.

2
00:00:10.375 --> 00:00:20.402
Open Operations, and choose the Shifts tab. Everyone starts on My shifts: whether you’re on duty now, your shifts coming up, and the hours planned and worked this week.

3
00:00:21.423 --> 00:00:30.938
Managers plan the week in Team schedule. There’s a row for each person, and every shift is colored by how it went: worked, late, missed, or still to come.

4
00:00:31.963 --> 00:00:39.792
On the right, planned hours sit next to the hours actually worked. Use the arrows to move week by week, or pick one location.

5
00:00:40.816 --> 00:00:52.549
To plan a shift, click Add shift, and pick the person, the location, and the times. Copy last week fills in the whole week, and with Training on, Worklynq checks everyone’s certifications first.

6
00:00:53.568 --> 00:01:05.067
On the day, people start, pause, and end their own shifts from the On duty now strip in Operations, or by telling Assist, start my shift. If you use Square, they’re clocked in and out there too.

7
00:01:06.087 --> 00:01:11.463
That’s Shifts. Next, the Daily brief: yesterday across every location, on one screen.

